# Environment settings for the Xymon client.

XYMSRV="@XYMONHOSTIP@"          # IP address of the Xymon server
XYMSERVERS=""                   # IP of multiple Xymon servers. XYMSRV must be "0.0.0.0".
CONFIGCLASS="$SERVEROSTYPE"     # Default configuration class for logfiles

PATH="/bin:/usr/bin:/sbin:/usr/sbin:/etc"  # PATH setting for the client scripts.
SHELL="/bin/sh"				# Shell to use when forking programs

# You normally don't need to modify anything below here
XYMONDPORT="1984"                   # Portnumber where xymond listens
XYMONHOME="$XYMONCLIENTHOME"       # Directory for the Xymon client files
XYMON="$XYMONHOME/bin/xymon"          # The Xymon client "xymon" utility
XYMONTMP="$XYMONHOME/tmp"             # Where we may store temporary files.
XYMONCLIENTLOGS="$XYMONHOME/logs"     # Where we store the client logfiles

# Options to logfetch, the xymon binary which examines log files for recent changes.
LOGFETCHOPTS=""


# Filesystem reporting -- the XYMONCLIENT_FS_* settings control df/inode data on
# the Linux, FreeBSD, NetBSD, OpenBSD and macOS clients. The three variables and
# the INCLUDE/EXCLUDE precedence (EXCLUDE wins) are the same on every OS; only the
# defaults and the exclusion mechanism differ:
#   - Linux: drops nodev pseudo types from /proc/filesystems (except rootfs);
#     INCLUDE="zfs virtiofs tmpfs", EXCLUDE="iso9660 squashfs fuse.snapfuse";
#     df -l. (Noisy /run* tmpfs are filtered server-side in analysis.cfg.)
#   - FreeBSD/NetBSD/OpenBSD: exclude a built-in pseudo-type set via df
#     "-t no<csv>"; INCLUDE/EXCLUDE default empty (they tune that set); df -l.
#   - macOS: filters mount(8) output (drops nobrowse/read-only); INCLUDE/EXCLUDE
#     default empty; DF_LOCAL_ONLY keeps only "local" (MNT_LOCAL) mounts.
# The per-variable text below describes the Linux defaults.
#
# XYMONCLIENT_FS_INCLUDE_TYPES: nodev FS types to surface that would otherwise be
#    dropped. Defaults to "zfs virtiofs tmpfs" (real local filesystems that
#    happen to be nodev). Set "" to drop every nodev type as before; add remote
#    types (e.g. "nfs nfs4 ceph") only with DF_LOCAL_ONLY=no, since df -l hides
#    remote mounts.
#
# XYMONCLIENT_FS_EXCLUDE_TYPES: FS types to exclude on top of the nodev default.
#    Defaults to "iso9660 squashfs fuse.snapfuse" -- read-only images always 100%
#    full by design. Matched on the exact df type token; nodev types are already
#    dropped, so useful entries name a non-nodev type (a device-backed type or a
#    specific FUSE subtype). If a type is in both lists, EXCLUDE wins.
#
# XYMONCLIENT_FS_DF_LOCAL_ONLY: "yes" (default) passes -l to df, hiding remote
#    filesystems; "no" reports nfs/ceph/etc; any other value warns and uses yes.
#    WARNING: with "no", a stale/hard-blocked remote mount can wedge df forever
#    (uninterruptible D-state): the client never finishes, so the whole host goes
#    PURPLE -- no data for ALL metrics, not just disk -- until it recovers or
#    reboots. A df that *exits* non-zero with no output is marked failed (yellow),
#    not left empty; this does NOT cover the hang (a wedged df never exits).
#
# XYMONCLIENT_FS_INCLUDE_TYPES="zfs virtiofs tmpfs"
# XYMONCLIENT_FS_EXCLUDE_TYPES="iso9660 squashfs fuse.snapfuse"
# XYMONCLIENT_FS_DF_LOCAL_ONLY="yes"


# Local Mode (Only) Options
#
# Running the Xymon client in local-config mode will cause threshold evaluation to
# be performed locally rather than sending raw data sent to the Xymon server for
# analysis. Only the processed results will be forwarded to your Xymon server.
# 
# This can also be overridden by adding a "--local" option to xymonclient.sh in
# the $XYMONHOME/etc/clientlaunch.cfg file
LOCALMODE="no"

# Local config for xymond_client (Ignored when not in local mode)
# This file is in the same format as analysis.cfg(5) on the Xymon server
LOCAL_CLIENTCONFIG="$XYMONHOME/etc/localclient.cfg"

# Local config for logfetch (Ignored when not in local mode)
# If not present, any saved server-side configs will be used
LOCAL_LOGFETCHCFG="$XYMONHOME/etc/logfetch.cfg"

# Local options for xymond_client (Ignored when not in local mode)
LOCAL_CLIENTOPTS=""


# Compatibility settings
HOBBITCLIENTHOME="$XYMONCLIENTHOME"

BBDISP="$XYMSRV"
BBDISPLAYS="$XYMSERVERS"

BBPORT="$XYMONDPORT"
BBHOME="$XYMONHOME"
BB="$XYMON"
BBTMP="$XYMONTMP"
BBCLIENTLOGS="$XYMONCLIENTLOGS"
